Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-usb2: acquire optional VBUS supply as optional

The binding does not require vbus-supply and the power callbacks already
support an absent regulator. Use the optional consumer API so that absence
does not create a dummy regulator. Propagate actual supplier errors rather
than silently ignoring everything except probe deferral.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-usb2.c b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-usb2.c
--- a/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/samsung/phy-samsung-usb2.c
@@ -212,9 +212,10 @@ static int samsung_usb2_phy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
-	drv->vbus = devm_regulator_get(dev, "vbus");
+	drv->vbus = devm_regulator_get_optional(dev, "vbus");
 	if (IS_ERR(drv->vbus)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(drv->vbus);
-		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
-			return ret;
+		if (ret != -ENODEV)
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
+					     "Failed to get VBUS supply\n");
 		drv->vbus = NULL;
 	}
 
 	for (i = 0; i < drv->cfg->num_phys; i++) {
